  said: Every dragon type that drops dragon bones does so at a **1/1 rate** (guaranteed), so any dragon task works. Here's the breakdown:

| Task | Slayer master(s) | Weight |
|---|---|---|
| Green dragons (incl. Brutal green) | Vannaka | 6 |
| Blue dragons | Vannaka / Chaeldar | 7 / 8 |
| Bronze dragons | Chaeldar | 11 |
| Iron dragons | Chaeldar / Duradel | 12 / 5 |
| Steel dragons | Duradel | 7 |
| Black dragons (incl. King Black Dragon) | Duradel | 9 |
| Mithril dragons | Duradel | 9 |

Two things worth noting: **Red dragons** is a task in the data but no master is recorded as assigning it, and the other two dragon-bone droppers — **Jogre** (1/128) and **Dragon impling** (1/20) — aren't tied to any Slayer task at all.

Best bets: **Chaeldar** for iron dragons (weight 12, the highest of any dragon-bone task), or **Vannaka** for green/blue dragons at lower levels; **Duradel** covers the high-end black, steel and mithril dragons.

